From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a find next starts from the active match

A find next is sent to the focused frame, and failing that to the first
frame with matches in the direction asked. A shell's find box is in the
shell's document, outside every frame of the guest being searched, so
`CheckFrame` refuses the focused frame and every find next fell back to
`GetInitialFrame`: forward happened to work, from the main frame, and
backward started over from the LAST frame -- a page whose last match is
in a cross-site <iframe> stepped from match 2 of 3 to 3 of 3 on "find
previous". guard-webview-find.sh read exactly that.

The frame holding the active match is where a find next means to start
from, so it is tried after the focused frame and before the first. A
browser whose find bar leaves the page's frame focused -- Chrome's --
never reaches it, so nothing there changes.

No other patch in the series touches this file, so its pre-image is the
pin's.
---
 content/browser/find_request_manager.cc | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/content/browser/find_request_manager.cc b/content/browser/find_request_manager.cc
index 9fbcd51..2c9abf7 100644
--- a/content/browser/find_request_manager.cc
+++ b/content/browser/find_request_manager.cc
@@ -685,11 +685,17 @@ void FindRequestManager::FindInternal(const FindRequest& request) {
     DCHECK_EQ(request.search_text, current_request_.search_text);
 
     // The find next request will be directed at the focused frame if there is
-    // one, or the first frame with matches otherwise.
+    // one, then at the frame holding the active match, or the first frame with
+    // matches otherwise. The active match's frame matters when focus is
+    // outside every frame searched -- an embedder's find box over a guest --
+    // where starting from the first frame would step backward from the last
+    // frame rather than from the active match.
     auto* focused_web_contents = contents_->GetFocusedWebContents();
     RenderFrameHost* target_rfh = focused_web_contents
                                       ? focused_web_contents->GetFocusedFrame()
                                       : nullptr;
+    if (!target_rfh || !CheckFrame(target_rfh))
+      target_rfh = active_frame_.get();
     if (!target_rfh || !CheckFrame(target_rfh))
       target_rfh = GetInitialFrame(request.options->forward);
 
